// Production (WP6.5, docs/rules/production.md): the two tuning numbers of the factory queues.
// Read by sf_data::production; sf_bridge::production_rules hands them to the world
// (World::with_production). What each unit costs and how long it takes is in unit_defs.ron
// (`cost`, `build_seconds`); which factory builds it follows from its category (infantry from the
// infantry factory, vehicles from the vehicle factory, vessels from the vessel factory); a unit may
// list structures that must stand first in `requires`. Placeholders for the balance rounds of
// phase 15 and the playtest of M1.
(
    // Most items in one factory's queue, the one being built included (1 to 20).
    queue_limit: 5,
    // How far, in cells (chessboard distance), from the cell next to the middle of the exit side a
    // finished unit looks for a free spot: ring 0 is the exit cell itself, then rings of growing
    // distance, each row by row from the north-west (1 to 8). If every cell in reach is blocked the
    // unit waits inside and the queue holds. 4 cells is a square of 9 by 9 round the exit.
    exit_radius: 4,
)
